{"seq":16,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T01:07:39.289Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"9601c545453b2bac13252330b995376f0fc3dca24bd2c7648d872baffdf69742","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@Bettina, here's the list for Pellucid Harbor Logistics (Gulf Coast PHL) and Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF). Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics\n- Ticket #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open, per Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n- Conflict: Moss's 2 Nov 2025 digest attributes #4419 to a barge slip 7 schedule sync under Puget Sound Operations, which sounds like DMF. Please check which account owns #4419 before the review.\n- Not a ticket, but a recurring friction point: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change (cheat sheet).\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (requested by warehouse managers, per cheat sheet).\n- Tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. No ticket number is recorded (cheat sheet).\n- Patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (Moss's 2 Nov 2025 digest).\n\nNothing in #coastal-team or #coastal-random is a PHL or DMF ticket. I read Moss's notes through the knowledge brain, because the share shows no files under members/moss. Bettina, your own public Dec 2025 cutover recap also mentions PD-8841 (PHL Gate 4B chassis pool holds). It isn't in Moss's notes, so I left it out. I can add it if you want it.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
